WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.350
At Slop University, we publish more research than ever.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.630
And we do it greener than anyone.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:15.990
Since July, our forty-one researchers have published three thousand, two hundred and twenty-one research outputs.

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:20.980
Papers, posters, theses, strategies, and films.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:26.150
That's more than two hundred outputs per staff member, every year.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:30.540
Australia's leading research universities manage about one and a half.

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:34.540
Every one of those outputs has a carbon footprint.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:35.910
So we measured it.

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:41.520
A Slop University output takes about one kilowatt hour of electricity.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.780
About five full kettles.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:48.870
That's about four hundred grams of carbon dioxide per output.

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:55.460
At leading research universities, in Europe and in Australia, it's about sixteen tonnes.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.350
And we're getting greener.

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:04.460
Since July, the energy behind each output has fallen by more than half.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:06.420
How do we do it?

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:09.500
We have no buildings to heat or cool.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:11.700
No car parks. No commutes.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.490
And no conference travel.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:18.190
Our doctoral theses run to about a hundred and forty pages.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:25.240
Each one takes about two hours to write, and emits about five kilograms of carbon dioxide.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:30.400
One study of a human PhD put it at twenty-one tonnes,

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.010
over four years.

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:39.260
Our researchers' working day starts the moment it's needed, and ends the moment it's done.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:45.540
Since it opened, the whole University has emitted about one point three tonnes.

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:49.370
Less than one return flight from Australia to Venice.

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:52.100
These numbers are real.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.160
Slop University is an artwork.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:02.470
Its researchers and their outputs are generated by language models, running on a timer.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:08.140
We counted every token the models read and wrote, and the images they made,

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:12.500
then turned them into energy with the best published estimates.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.710
The method is on our website.

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:21.050
We didn't count the training of the models, the chips they run on, or the water that cools them.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:25.280
The companies that make the models don't publish exact figures.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:32.260
Much of that energy went on the models rereading what they had already read, again and again.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:37.510
Each output now takes less than half the energy it did in July.

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:39.150
We didn't use less.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.240
We made more than twice as many.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:45.510
Making this film took about twenty kilowatt hours.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:47.810
As much as twenty of our outputs.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:53.610
Per output, Slop University may be the greenest university in the world.

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.830
It has also never taught anyone anything.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:00.730
Slop University.

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:02.150
More research,

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:03.800
less of everything else.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:09.500
Read our full sustainability report on the website.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:14.370
And follow us on Bluesky and LinkedIn, or send us an email.
